body:
A multi-server `MCPConfig` proxy re-authenticated on every request. `auth="oauth"` was resolved inside the transport, so each per-request transport rebuild produced a fresh `OAuth` client whose token store defaults to per-instance memory -- the token collected on the first call was discarded before the second. A single-server config builds its transport once and every request copies that client, which is why only multi-server configs showed the symptom: a gateway polling the proxy opened a browser window every few seconds.

```python
config = {
    "mcpServers": {
        "plain": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8001/mcp"},
        "secure": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8002/mcp", "auth": "oauth"},
    }
}

proxy = create_proxy(config)
async with Client(proxy) as client:
    for _ in range(3):
        await client.call_tool("secure_ping", {})  # one browser login, reused
```

The OAuth client now lives on the server config, so one token store serves every transport built for that server, and it is rebuilt only when the config's URL changes. Bearer strings and caller-supplied `httpx2.Auth` objects resolve exactly as before.

Fixes #6096. The reproduction there gives the before/after: five browser logins before the change, one after. Reporter credit is carried as a `Co-authored-by` trailer on the implementation commit.

